WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.880
Everything in lipid synthesis begins with a single two-carbon unit, acetyl-CoA,

2
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:13.440
and from that one starting point, the cell builds three completely different kinds

3
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:19.260
of molecules. It can pour carbons into storage fats, the triacylglycerols that bank

4
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.200
energy. It can route them into membranes, the phospholipids and sphingolipids that

5
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.220
wrap every cell, or it can elaborate them into hormones and signaling molecules like

6
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.580
cholesterol and steroids.

7
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.380
The same carbons, three destinations.

8
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.140
What decides the fate is not the raw material, but the regulatory switches, whether

9
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.600
you are fed or fasting, flush with energy or starving, and how much cholesterol you

10
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.600
already hold.

11
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.080
Cholesterol is an enormous biosynthetic feat.

12
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.140
Every one of its 27 carbons traces back to the same humble two-carbon unit, acetyl

13
00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:01.060
-CoA. Eighteen acetyl-CoA molecules are pooled and condensed, and 27 of those

14
00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.100
carbons are retained in the final sterol.

15
00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:08.900
The assembly happens in three broad stages and roughly 30 enzymatic steps, first

16
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:13.740
building activated isoprene units, then chaining them into the 30-carbon squalene,

17
00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.760
then folding and trimming squalene into cholesterol.

18
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.100
The takeaway is conceptual, not arithmetic.

19
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.420
A molecule this structurally rich is built entirely from small, identical bricks,

20
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.280
which is exactly why its synthesis is so energetically expensive and so heavily

21
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:31.280
regulated.

22
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.400
HMG-CoA reductase is the rate-limiting enzyme of cholesterol synthesis and the

23
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:42.040
target of statins, so the cell guards it with four independent control layers

24
00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.160
operating on different time scales.

25
00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:50.580
Fastest is phosphorylation by AMPK, which switches the enzyme off within seconds to

26
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.020
minutes when energy is low.

27
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.660
Slower is translational control, where mevalonate-derived products suppress the

28
00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.880
messenger RNA over minutes to hours.

29
00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:06.160
Slower still is transcriptional control through SREBP, tuning enzyme amount over

30
00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:11.180
hours, and finally, sterile-induced degradation accelerates destruction of the

31
00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.640
protein itself. Four dials, one enzyme.

32
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:20.220
Cholesterol is essential but toxic in excess, so the cell never relies on a single

33
00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.220
switch.

34
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.040
Think of cholesterol synthesis as a thermostat with two sensors feeding one dial.

35
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.440
SREBP senses cholesterol itself.

36
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.060
When the membrane runs low on cholesterol, SREBP turns synthesis up.

37
00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.360
AMPK senses energy.

38
00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:44.200
When ATP runs low and AMP rises, AMPK turns synthesis down because you should not

39
00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.260
spend fuel building expensive molecules during a famine.

40
00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:53.060
The two inputs converge on a single set point, balancing supply against both demand

41
00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.060
and affordability.

42
00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.640
High cholesterol pushes the needle toward less synthesis.

43
00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.940
Low energy does the same for a different reason.

44
00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.040
The cell is not maximizing cholesterol.

45
00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.220
It is matching production precisely to need.

46
00:03:08.083 --> 00:03:14.303
AMPK is the cell's low-fuel warning light, and it reads the AMP to ATP ratio

47
00:03:14.303 --> 00:03:20.583
directly. When that ratio climbs, signaling a low-energy state, AMPK becomes active

48
00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:24.283
and starts phosphorylating the expensive biosynthetic enzymes.

49
00:03:24.863 --> 00:03:30.943
It shuts down HMG-CoA reductase, halting cholesterol synthesis, and it inactivates

50
00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:35.003
acetyl-CoA carboxylase, halting fatty acid synthesis.

51
00:03:35.463 --> 00:03:37.343
The logic is blunt and sensible.

52
00:03:38.043 --> 00:03:43.443
Do not spend ATP building storage and membrane molecules when you do not have ATP to

53
00:03:43.443 --> 00:03:45.703
spare. This is metabolic triage.

54
00:03:46.183 --> 00:03:51.703
Energy charge is monitored continuously, and the moment reserves dip, AMPK pulls the

55
00:03:51.703 --> 00:03:54.643
brake on anabolism across multiple pathways at once.
